# 2. Project Overview

The Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture (AVIA) is a systems engineering project dedicated to the research, design, development, and validation of an adaptive vehicle architecture that enhances vehicle operation through intelligent coordination of vehicle subsystems.

Rather than focusing on isolated vehicle components, AVIA approaches the vehicle as an integrated engineering system in which mechanical, electrical, electronic, computational, and human-interaction elements operate together to achieve coordinated, adaptive, and efficient performance.

The project emphasizes a solution-independent engineering methodology. Engineering objectives are established before solutions are proposed, ensuring that design decisions remain traceable to clearly defined needs, constraints, and system requirements.

AVIA is intended to provide a structured engineering framework that supports the systematic investigation, development, and validation of adaptive vehicle technologies while maintaining safety, reliability, maintainability, scalability, and engineering integrity throughout the project lifecycle.
